<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  HealthKit entitlement, written by hand because there is no Mac on which to tick the
	  capability box in Xcode. Xcode normally does two things at once here: it writes this
	  file, and it enables HealthKit on the App ID in Apple's developer portal.

	  This file is only the first half. The App ID must also have HealthKit enabled at
	  developer.apple.com › Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles › Identifiers › com.varun.ignyt,
	  which is a browser page and needs no Mac. Without that, signing fails with a message
	  about the provisioning profile not including the com.apple.developer.healthkit
	  entitlement — which reads like a certificate problem and is not one.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
	<true/>
	<!--
	  Declares which HealthKit data classes the app touches. Clinical records are deliberately
	  absent: IGNYT reads fitness data only, and requesting clinical access would trigger a
	  much heavier App Store review for a capability the app never uses.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.healthkit.access</key>
	<array/>
	<!--
	  Sign in with Apple. The same two-halves problem as HealthKit above, and the same failure
	  if only one half is done: "Sign in with Apple" must ALSO be enabled on the App ID at
	  developer.apple.com › Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles › Identifiers › com.varun.ignyt.

	  Until it is, this file asks for an entitlement the provisioning profile cannot contain and
	  SIGNING FAILS OUTRIGHT — not just Apple sign-in, the whole build. That is worth knowing
	  because the error names the entitlement and reads like a certificate problem.

	  "Default" is the standard value: sign-in through the app itself. The other value, an
	  associated web domain, is only for a website sharing the same account system.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
